BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Come From Away: Marin's First Production of the Tony-Winning Music
 al
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:2611080s6CzmDqakiGIXV0tYkOKQ
DESCRIPTION:A Tony-winning Broadway hit is coming to San Anselmo\, and it'
 s the first time it's ever been performed in Marin.\n\n**Come From Away**\
 n\nBook\, Music and Lyrics by Irene Sankoff and David Hein\n\nOn 9/11\, 38
  planes were suddenly grounded in a tiny town in Newfoundland. Overnight\,
  the locals took in nearly 7\,000 stranded travelers from around the world
 \, and strangers became family. This is their true story\, and it's funny\
 , uplifting and full of heart\, with a live band of musicians from Marin's
  Irish music scene.\n\nSan Domenico School's production marks the 25th ann
 iversary of 9/11.\n\nShow times:\n\n**Friday\, November 13 at 7pm**\n\n**S
 aturday\, November 14 at 1pm and 7pm**\n\n**Sunday\, November 15 at 3pm**\
 n\nTickets: $15 general\, $10 students and seniors\n\nRun time: About 2 ho
 urs\, including intermission\n\nFree parking. Wheelchair accessible.\n\n**
 Saturday night still has the best seats!**\n\n*Please be advised that adul
 t language and the mention of difficult subject matter\, including Islamop
 hobia and 9/11\, are included in this show.*\n\nCome From Away is presente
 d through special arrangement with Music Theatre International (MTI). MTI 
 also supplies all authorized performance materials. www.MTIShows.com
LOCATION:Carol Franc Buck Hall of the Arts\, San Domenico School
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/san-domenico-upper-school-presents-come-f
 rom-away-tickets-2003472917428
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
