BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blithe Spirit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
UID:261104qtUsUTKOO0iuL2JeZFSTIw
DESCRIPTION:A ghostly comedy filled with unexpected twists\, supernatural 
 surprises\, and plenty of laughs is coming to the San Marin stage!\n\nSan 
 Marin Performing Arts is excited to present Blithe Spirit\, the classic co
 medy by celebrated playwright Noël Coward. Running November 12–16 at th
 e Emily Gates Performing Arts Center\, this witty and spirited production 
 brings together mystery\, mischief\, and a little supernatural chaos\, all
  brought to life by San Marin High School's talented drama students.\n\nAb
 out the Show\n\nWhat happens when a séance goes hilariously wrong?\n\nNov
 elist Charles Condomine invites the eccentric medium Madame Arcati to his 
 home\, hoping to gather inspiration for his next book. But when the séanc
 e unexpectedly summons the ghost of his first wife\, Elvira\, things quick
 ly spiral out of control.\n\nInvisible to everyone but Charles\, the misch
 ievous Elvira is determined to disrupt his marriage to his second wife\, R
 uth. As supernatural surprises and romantic rivalries unfold\, Charles fin
 ds himself caught between two wives\, one living and one very much not.\n\
 nFilled with sharp dialogue\, clever humor\, and delightfully chaotic situ
 ations\, Blithe Spirit is a timeless comedy that proves some relationships
  are difficult to leave behind\, even after death.\n\nMeet the Cast\n\nFli
 nt Berberich as Charles Condomine\n\nJade Stanton as Ruth Condomine\n\nDev
 yn Lawrence-Hall as Elvira Condomine\n\nBella Lessig as Madame Arcati\n\nG
 iselle De Leon as Dr. George Bradman\n\nCatania DeKeyrel as Mrs. Violet Br
 adman\n\nCailey Gettle and Amiya Clark as Edith\n\nPerformance Dates & Tim
 es\n\nJoin us for one of four performances:\n\nThursday\, November 12 — 
 7:00 PM\n\nFriday\, November 13 — 7:00 PM\n\nSunday\, November 15 — 2:
 00 PM\n\nMonday\, November 16 — 7:00 PM\n\nLocation: Emily Gates Perform
 ing Arts Center\, San Marin High School\, Novato\, CA\n\nCo-Directed by Br
 ad Smith and Linda Kislingbury\n\nTickets & Admission\n\nGeneral Admission
 : $5 Students / $10 Adults General seating / Opening Seating. No reserved 
 seats.\n\nTickets will be available for purchase at the door beginning one
  hour before each performance. Come enjoy an entertaining evening \\(or af
 ternoon!\\) of live theater while supporting the talented student actors a
 nd crew who bring this spirited comedy to the stage. We look forward to se
 eing you there!
LOCATION:Emily Gates Performing Arts Center - San Marin High
URL:https://www.sanmarinperformingarts.org/news-highlights/blithe-spirit
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artazan Handcraft Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:261104Fnsjyinb40eWNTWqi6uqjg
DESCRIPTION:Artazan Handcraft Market returns to Pasadena November 14–15\
 , bringing together artists\, artisans\, craftspeople and the community fo
 r a weekend celebrating creativity and work made by hand.\n\nInspired by t
 he ideas behind the Arts & Crafts movement\, the handcraft market celebrat
 es creativity\, thoughtful design\, skilled work and the people behind the
  things we bring into our lives. That spirit is reflected in a contemporar
 y and wide-ranging mix of handcraft\, encompassing many different material
 s\, traditions and creative approaches.\n\nHeld at the Pasadena Convention
  Center\, the two-day market will be filled with work from independent art
 ists and artisans across an eclectic mix of mediums. Visitors might discov
 er jewelry and metalsmithing\, ceramics and glass\, crochet and fiber art\
 , woodworking and handcrafted clocks\, painting and mixed media\, wearable
  art\, leatherwork\, home décor\, artisan foods and much more. From time-
 honored skills to unexpected new ideas\, the market reflects the remarkabl
 e variety of what people are creating by hand today.\n\nThe weekend will a
 lso connect with Pasadena’s broader creative community\, bringing togeth
 er local and regional artists\, arts organizations\, educators and visitor
 s. Guests can talk directly with artists\, learn about their materials and
  techniques\, take part in hands-on workshops\, watch demonstrations and e
 njoy live music throughout the weekend.\n\nTaking place at the beginning o
 f the holiday season\, the November market offers an alternative to mass-p
 roduced holiday shopping\, with distinctive gifts\, original art\, artisan
  foods and objects for the home\, while directly supporting independent ar
 tists and small creative businesses.\n\nMore than a place to shop\, Artaza
 n offers an opportunity to see handcraft up close\, discover something une
 xpected and experience the incredible range of things being made by hand t
 oday.\n\nEVENT DETAILS Artazan Handcraft Market November 14–15\, 2026 Pa
 sadena Convention Center • Pasadena\, California Saturday & Sunday • 1
 0 a.m.–5 p.m.\n\nTickets\, workshops\, exhibitor information and additio
 nal details are available at Artazan.com.
LOCATION:Pasadena Convention Center
URL:https://www.artazan.com/pasadena.php
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Mirror: Stage Play
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T173000
UID:261103w9xWuBiVYU6XU-yPnla_fw
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for an unforgettable evening of drama and excitement
  with The Mirror Stage play. The Mirror is a one-man play that takes you i
 nside the mind of James\, a man caught between his present and past selves
 . In a series of intimate conversations with his reflection\, James confro
 nts his inner self\, the protective voice that has shielded him from pain\
 , rejection\, and vulnerability throughout his life. But James wants more.
  He wants to live openly\, to take risks\, to love & feel deeply\, even if
  it means getting hurt. His inner self resists\, clinging to the walls he'
 s built around himself. Through their dialogue\, they explore relationship
 s that never quite worked\, career choices driven by fear rather than pass
 ion and commitment\, and the triggers and traumas that shaped James.
LOCATION:Sir Winston Event House
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-mirror-stage-play-tickets-20006613960
 92
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Richard Heinberg: A Celebration of His Life and Legacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:261103IP4rwZ-ND0eFoVAKEFqwiA
DESCRIPTION:***Author • Musician • Senior Fellow at Post Carbon Instit
 ute • Environmental Educator • Artist • Husband • Friend***\n\nYou
  are warmly invited to join family\, friends\, colleagues\, and admirers f
 rom around the world on **November 15th** as we come together to celebrate
  the extraordinary life and legacy of **Richard Heinberg**.\n\nA Senior Fe
 llow at Post Carbon Institute for nearly 20 years\, Richard was a pioneeri
 ng voice on resilience and the energy crisis. He was the author of fourtee
 n books\, hundreds of articles\, and the award-winning monthly *Museletter
 .*\n\nRichard was a skilled writer and speaker who could synthesize comple
 x issues and ideas into understandable language. His calm demeanor\, sharp
  wit\, and intense focus made difficult and daunting facts feel bearable.\
 n\nRichard was a lifelong violinist and guitarist who\, more recently\, to
 ok up the piano. For decades\, he maintained a devoted\, focused daily pra
 ctice and played in bands\, chamber groups\, duos\, and orchestras through
 out his life.\n\nBeyond his public work\, those who knew him personally we
 re struck by his genuine curiosity. He was always asking questions and tru
 ly listening for the answers.  \n\nJoin us in Santa Rosa on November 15th
  for an afternoon of gratitude and celebration for a life so fully and gen
 erously lived. Richard’s commemoration will be held from 2:30 to 4:00 pm
 \, with arrival starting at 2:00 pm and a social hour to follow the progra
 m.\n\nPlease use the RSVP link on EverLoved to let us know if you plan on 
 attending.
LOCATION:The Glaser Center
URL:https://everloved.com/life-of/richard-heinberg/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Misner & Smith Matinee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
UID:261031bVUi234JjUSUChsP-7EO-Q
DESCRIPTION:Misner & Smith's music is a rare combination of poetic\, story
 -filled songwriting lifted to exquisite heights by masterful vocal harmoni
 es.\n\nFollowing the release of their critically acclaimed new album\, All
  is Song\, Northern California-based unclassifiable duo Misner & Smith ret
 urn to HopMonk Sebastopol - The Abbey - for another evening of masterful v
 ocal harmonies and extraordinary songwriting. With All is Song they turn i
 n their finest work to date--an album of inspired declarations to the powe
 r of music\, song\, and collaboration. Their live shows are no different\,
  and the beauty of their vocal harmonies combined with truly inventive son
 gwriting has made the band one of the most inspiring acts in the Americana
  world. Blending elements of that genre with rock\, traditional folk\, and
  more pop-leaning ideas\, Misner & Smith makes music gloriously nonconform
 ing.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040036054?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
