BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Sourdough Baking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T164500
UID:261031SWe7JX9QhES3Gpuvmewefw
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, November 15\, 2026 2:00 pm to 4:45 pm Room 110\n\nCat
 egory\n\nCulinary Arts\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and
  older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$5\n\nTotal Regi
 stration Cost:\n\n$105\n\nDelve into the delicious art of sourdough baking
  with our hands-on workshop that aims to demystify the sourdough process a
 nd make it more approachable for at-home bakers! This hands-on experience 
 will guide you through each step of the process\, deepening your understan
 ding of the fundamentals of sourdough and elevating your baking skills to 
 new heights! Learn the secrets behind cultivating and maintaining a robust
  starter culture and the key to a deliciously tangy bread.Next\, roll up y
 our sleeves as you learn to mix\, knead\, and shape your dough like a pro.
  Gain insight into the science behind fermentation and gluten development 
 and discover the secrets to achieving that perfect rise and flavor. We’l
 l dive into various techniques for shaping your loaves\, from classic roun
 ds to unique designs.Learn how to customize your sourdough with unique ing
 redients\, adding a personal touch to your creations. You’ll also explor
 e different scoring methods to achieve beautiful patterns on your bread. E
 ach participant will leave with a starter culture to kickstart their sourd
 ough journey\, their own ready-to-bake boule\, and the confidence to bake 
 their own sourdough!
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-sourdough-b
 aking-november/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crepe Paper Flowers: Poinsettia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T143000
UID:261031RFJiGNaMdE-0HYYxbEu8og
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, November 15\, 2026 10:00 am to 2:30 pm\n\nLocation\n\
 nRoom 201\, Fiber Arts Studio\n\nCategory\n\nFiber Arts\n\nExperience Leve
 l\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$75\n\nMat
 erials Fee:\n\n$5\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$80\n\nCreate a beautiful
 \, lifelike poinsettia using delicate crepe paper\, shaped petals\, and ca
 refully crafted details. Each petal is cut\, stretched\, and formed by han
 d to capture the natural curves and rich colors of this classic Christmas 
 flower. Layer the petals around a cluster of tiny yellow centers\, add gre
 en paper leaves\, and gently shape each piece to bring the flower to life.
  The finished poinsettia makes a lovely handmade decoration for the holida
 y season\, perfect for wreaths\, centerpieces\, gift wrapping\, or festive
  home décor.Perfect for beginners and flower lovers alike\, this workshop
  offers a relaxing and creative experience where you’ll leave with your 
 own handmade poinsettia to enjoy or gift.No previous experience is require
 d—all materials and step-by-step instruction are provided. Please bring 
 a bag lunch or snacks and a beverage/water bottle.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/crepe-paper-flowers-poinset
 tia/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
