BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Standing Tall: The Story of the Mare Island 21ers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T210000
UID:261110g-JBW5mji0yZ2kjJodW8wQ
DESCRIPTION:On November 17\, 1961\, twenty-one Black workers at the Mare I
 sland Naval Shipyard did something few people dared: They filed a formal c
 omplaint of racial discrimination against the United States government.\n\
 nThey were pipefitters\, mechanics\, welders\, painters\, and laborers who
  had endured years of unequal treatment in hiring\, training\, promotions\
 , and pay. They filed their complaint before the Civil Rights Act of 1964 
 and before the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission existed. They put t
 heir jobs on the line anyway. Represented by attorney Charles Wilson\, the
 y pressed their case against the federal government at a time when few wou
 ld\, and their stand helped build the pressure that changed federal employ
 ment law.\n\nSixty-five years later\, the Vallejo Naval & Historical Museu
 m marks the anniversary with an evening of living history\, right here in 
 the city where it happened. Opening Remarks\n\nScott Stick\, Audio Visual 
 Archivist for the Vallejo Naval & Historical Museum\, will open the evenin
 g.\n\nModerator: Brendan Riley\, Vallejo historian and longtime Associated
  Press reporter Panelists\n\nJake Sloan\, the youngest of the Original 21e
 rs and author of Standing Tall: Willie Long vs. U.S. Government at Mare Is
 land Naval Shipyard. Pastor Anthony Gilmore\, who took the initiative to t
 alk with his uncle\, Original 21er Clarence Williams\, then brought that s
 tory to Matthias Gafni at the Vallejo Times-Herald. Matthias Gafni\, now a
  reporter for the San Francisco Chronicle\, wrote a detailed three-part se
 ries on the 21ers while at the Vallejo Times-Herald.\n\nWilhelmenia Wilson
  – Daughter of Charles Wilson\, the attorney for the 21ers. She is curre
 ntly the Executive Director of Healthy Black Families\, Inc. \\(www.health
 yblackfam.org\\)\n\nSharon McGriff-Payne\, a local historian who will spea
 k to the early African American experience in Solano County\, leading up t
 o and including Mare Island Naval Shipyard.\n\nTogether\, they'll trace ho
 w a story nearly lost to history was passed from one generation to the nex
 t\, from a nephew&\\#39\;s conversation with his uncle\, one of the origin
 al 21\, to the pages of a local newspaper\, to a book written by a man who
  was there. Schedule\n\n5:30 PM: Doors open 6:00 PM: Panel discussion 7:30
  PM: Q&A and book signing\n\nAdmission: Free\n\nSuggested donation of $25 
 per person\n\nSeating is limited\, so please RSVP to reserve your spot. Co
 pies of Standing Tall will be available for purchase.
LOCATION:Vallejo Naval and Historical Museum
URL:https://vallejomuseum.net/event/standing-tall-the-story-of-the-mare-is
 land-21ers/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Standing Tall: The Story of the Mare Island 21ers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T200000
UID:261109zAbQdv5GkUCK2JWE0pErOg
DESCRIPTION:A living history panel on the story of the Mare Island 21ers\,
  the Black shipyard workers who took on the U.S. Navy.\n\nOn November 17\,
  1961\, twenty-one Black workers at the Mare Island Naval Shipyard did som
 ething few people dared: They filed a formal complaint of racial discrimin
 ation against the United States government.\n\nThey were pipefitters\, mec
 hanics\, welders\, painters\, and laborers who had endured years of unequa
 l treatment in hiring\, training\, promotions\, and pay. They filed their 
 complaint before the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and before the Equal Employm
 ent Opportunity Commission existed. They put their jobs on the line anyway
 . Represented by attorney Charles Wilson\, they pressed their case against
  the federal government at a time when few would\, and their stand helped 
 build the pressure that changed federal employment law.\n\nSixty-five year
 s later\, the Vallejo Naval & Historical Museum marks the anniversary with
  an evening of living history\, right here in the city where it happened.\
 n\n**Opening Remarks**\n\n**Scott Stick**\, Audio Visual Archivist for the
  Vallejo Naval & Historical Museum\, will open the evening.\n\n**Moderator
 **: \n\n**Brendan Riley**\, Vallejo historian and longtime Associated Pre
 ss reporter\n\n**Panelists**\n\n**Jake Sloan**\, the youngest of the Origi
 nal 21ers and author of *Standing Tall: Willie Long vs. U.S. Government a
 t Mare Island Naval Shipyard*.\n\n**Pastor Anthony Gilmore**\, who took th
 e initiative to talk with his uncle\, Original 21er Clarence Williams\, th
 en brought that story to Matthias Gafni at the *Vallejo Times-Herald*.\n\
 n**Matthias Gafni**\, now a reporter for the *San Francisco Chronicle*\, 
 wrote a detailed three-part series on the 21ers while at the *Vallejo Tim
 es-Herald.*\n\n**Wilhelmenia Wilson** - Daughter of Charles Wilson\, the 
 attorney for the 21ers. She is currently the Executive Director of Healthy
  Black Families\, Inc. (www.healthyblackfam.org)\n\n**Sharon McGriff-Payne
 **\, a local historian who will speak to the early African American experi
 ence in Solano County\, leading up to and including Mare Island Naval Ship
 yard.\n\nTogether\, they'll trace how a story nearly lost to history was p
 assed from one generation to the next\, from a nephew's conversation with 
 his uncle\, one of the original 21\, to the pages of a local newspaper\, t
 o a book written by a man who was there.
LOCATION:Vallejo Naval and Historical Museum - Heritage Chamber
URL:https://bit.ly/JakeSloanVallejoMuseumEvent
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T220000
UID:261108B0Vr9u6YsUajqo9QqoQSMA
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\n**Trigger warnings:** Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in
  Yiddish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pendant Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T140000
UID:261106nMuwa2KoyUyQNe8pruZsmg
DESCRIPTION:In this class\, students will learn the art of weaving in a ci
 rcular pattern to create beautiful round pendants. Students will use raffi
 a or a large assortment of strings to create these woven spirals.\n\nYou w
 ill learn how to add columns\, change colors\, and finish your project in 
 this 4 hour workshop.\n\nAll materials will be provided.\n\nThese spirals 
 can be utilized as a wall piece\, or worn as a pendant!\n\nAbout the Teach
 er: Carrie Botto is a self taught multi medium weaver. She started weaving
  with beads over 40 years ago and continues to add skills and techniques t
 o her “tool box”. Carrie travels all over the country now teach severa
 l different classes\, and has taught at Mendocino Art Center\, New Mexico 
 Bead Trader\, Moab Art Center\, and Fiber on 4th in New Mexico. Follow Car
 rie on Instagram @beanstreetstudio!
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/pendant-workshop
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wreckless Strangers at Rancho Nicasio
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
UID:261106aTxePpIqBUiFaxK5ewdidA
DESCRIPTION:Riding high from their recent performance at **Hardly Strictl
 y Bluegrass**\, Ameri-Cali Soul band **Wreckless Strangers** are kicking
  off the holiday season with their first Christmas song\, “**Christmas 
 Tears**\,” arriving November 6. The band will debut the single live\, a
 longside its signature blend of originals and crowd-pleasing covers\, at 
 **Rancho Nicasio** on **Friday\, November 20**\, followed by a show at 
 **Lucca Bar & Grill** in **Benicia** on **Saturday\, December 19**.\n\nT
 he two performances bring Wreckless Strangers’ soulful\, roots-driven ro
 ck to two special corners of the Bay Area. On November 20\, the band takes
  the stage at **Rancho Nicasio**\, the historic West Marin roadhouse know
 n for live music\, dinner shows\, and its laid-back country setting. On De
 cember 19\, they perform at **Lucca Bar & Grill** in Benicia\, a waterfr
 ont town with a welcoming small-town feel and a lively dining and music sc
 ene.\n\nOriginally released by **Sonny Thompson and Robert Wilson** and 
 made famous by blues legend **Freddie King**\, “**Christmas Tears**” 
 takes on new life through Wreckless Strangers’ soul-driven arrangement\,
  old-school piano\, and emotionally charged vocals.\n\nRecorded at the leg
 endary **FAME Recording Studios in Muscle Shoals\, Alabama**\, the single
  offers a different perspective on the season. Rather than focusing on the
  usual joy and nostalgia\, the band leans into a more melancholy side of t
 he holidays\, with lead vocalist **Amber Morris** delivering a standout 
 performance that balances technical precision with the song’s raw emotio
 n.\n\nThe idea for the band’s first Christmas release had been circulati
 ng for years. In April\, while visiting Tennessee\, the band found a break
  between shows in Nashville and Knoxville and seized the opportunity to re
 cord at FAME Studios with producer **David Kalmusky\,** whose credits in
 clude Keith Urban\, Carrie Underwood\, Justin Bieber\, and Journey. It was
  Amber who suggested “Christmas Tears\,” an unconventional choice that
  proved to be the perfect fit.\n\n“Christmas Tears” will be available 
 on all streaming platforms on November 6.
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:http://ranchonicasio.com/events/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Olio Nuovo Harvest and Milling Experience at Gold Ridge Organic Fa
 rms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T141500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T153000
UID:261104hxWhxzxIlEKiDidqkKwSKw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an unforgettable behind-the-scenes journey into th
 e heart of our olive harvest season. This experience offers a rare opportu
 nity to see how our award-winning olive oil is crafted\, from the branches
  of our olive trees to the first drops of the season’s oil.\n\nYour jour
 ney begins with a guided tour of our 88-acre organic farm. You’ll step i
 nto the orchards to watch our expert team harvest fresh olives straight fr
 om the trees at their peak of flavor.\n\nNext\, you’ll visit our state-o
 f-the-art olive oil mill\, where you’ll learn about the milling process 
 and see the olives pressed into vibrant\, fresh Olio Nuovo\, the celebrate
 d “new oil” prized by culinary enthusiasts for its brilliant green hue
  and robust\, peppery finish.\n\nThe highlight comes right at the source: 
 tasting fresh Olio Nuovo straight from the mill just moments after the oli
 ves are crushed.\n\nBook now to secure your spot for this rare\, behind-th
 e-scenes look at our harvest traditions.\n\nImportant Notes: Please wear c
 omfortable shoes suitable for walking on a working farm This outdoor exper
 ience may be canceled due to wet weather. Full refund available.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/627571/olio
 -nuovo-harvest-and-milling-experience
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AURORA SINGH headlines Friday Night Comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T220000
UID:261103_tftK6YwEkWs9yNLlovR9w
DESCRIPTION:Friday night stand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa with Auror
 a Singh\n\nStand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nVIP TABLES NOW AVAILA
 BLE! Snag a table for 4 with preferred seating\, your own private call but
 ton to summon service\, and your first round of beer/cider (or a bottle of
  wine) for only $95! Every Friday night hilarious comedians from The Bay A
 rea and beyond perform at Barrel Proof Lounge. Stick around after for late
 -night karaoke!\n\nFresh lineup of funny each Friday.\n\nThis Week: Host: 
 Josh Argyle Noah Radke Drew Shafer\n\nHeadliner: Aurora Singh\n\nSome call
  her a rare breed\, I would agree. Aurora Singh blessed her immigrant pare
 nts with her arrival into the world in January 1992 and continuously douse
 d her sparkle upon the world as she grew up in Sacramento\, California in 
 the good ol’ Catholic school system. You won’t regret the deep belly l
 aughs you experience as a result of her hilarious straight forward real co
 medy. After 9 years of bringing the funny\, Aurora has been featured on Si
 rius XM\, ABC’s The 100K Pyramid and has performed with incredible comed
 ians such as Sheng Wang\, Greg Fitzsimons\, Anthony Jeselnik\, Roy Wood Jr
 . and Hasan Minhaj. She has also entered the college and cruise markets no
 w taking her reach nationally! Her mom has even been quoted saying\, “sh
 e’s hilarious!” Ready to ride the giggle train? All aboard! -Recurring
  feature at Laughs Unlimited Comedy Club in Sacramento\, CA. -Recurring Li
 ve Nation host: hosts at San Francisco Punch Line\, Sacramento Punch Line\
 , and Cobb's Comedy Club. -Recurring feature at Loonee’s Comedy Corner\,
  Colorado Springs\, CO. -Recurring host at Rooster T. Feathers Comedy Club
 \, Sunnyvale\, CA. -Recurring feature act for Mic Drop Comedy Club San Die
 go. -Headliner Laughingstock Comedy Club\, Bakersfield\, CA. -Showcase pro
 ducer with Live Nation at the Sacramento Punch Line. -Showcase producer at
  Sacramento Comedy Spot. -Accepted into Women in Comedy Festival 2020. -Wo
 rld Series of Comedy Semi-Finalist 2020. -Big Pine Comedy Festival “Best
  of Fest” award 2022. -Made virtual Chocolate Sundaes history by getting
  100% of the audience vote to move to the live show at the Hollywood Laugh
  Factory 2022. -Sac Town Comedy Get Down Festival “Best of Fest” 2022.
  -World Series of Comedy Semi-Finalist 2022 -World Series of Comedy Laughs
  Unlimited Semi-Finalist 2023 -Season 6 Episode 15 of the 100K Pyramid on 
 ABC and Hulu -APCA Comedian of the Year 2025 -Regular headlining act on No
 rwegian Cruise Lines Check out her website at **https://www.aurorasinghcom
 edy.com/**\n\n21+ Doors - 7p / Show - 8p $15adv / $20door\n\nCheck out **w
 ww.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/aurora-singh-headlines-friday-night-comed
 y-in-downtown-santa-rosa-tickets-2001405654188?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
