UID:261110JoUrNpcn-0aSd60DZVlkXg
DESCRIPTION:Vallejo local singer\, Joyce Grant returns to the Ferry Taproo
 m with her powerful mix of jazz\, blues\, and R&B.\n\n‍Joyce Grant singe
 r/songwriter\, is no stranger to Vallejo.  She performs regularly at the 
 Vallejo Ferry Bldg. Taproom\, the Coalshed as well as the Benicia Taphouse
 . A mezzo-soprano with a voice like dark honey\, Grant has been singing ja
 zz and R&B in the Bay Area for over 30 years at venues such the Donatello 
 Hotel in San Francisco\, the Ledson Hotel in Sonoma\, the Empress Theater 
 in Vallejo\, Sam’s Chowder House in Half Moon Bay\, Nick’s in Pacifica
  to name a few. She is the great-great-niece of famed ragtime composer Sco
 tt Joplin and is a frequent participant in the West Coast Ragtime festival
 .\n\nFor the past 3 years she has been the lead vocalist for the Walnut Cr
 eek Jazz Band\, an 18- piece big band. As a songwriter she has released th
 e CD In The Morning \\(co-produced with Doug McKeehan \, 2010\\)\, a colle
 ction of original songs ranging in style from jazz to blues to R&B. She co
 ntinues to bring her sensitive and powerful vocal interpretations to appre
 ciative audiences that keep coming back for more.
LOCATION:Ferry Taproom
URL:https://www.mareislandbrewingco.com/events/live-music-saturday-1121202
 6
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T220000
UID:261108ZeR7Df4y8Uq2L2j7IycZFA
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\n**Trigger warnings:** Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in
  Yiddish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Mayflower: An Interesting Mix of Passengers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T143000
UID:2611089SQd2Kq9pEez4Wegu12lug
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society Presents\n\n The Mayflo
 wer: An Interesting Mix of Passengers\n\n Presented by Suzanne Brayer\n\n 
 In 1620\, an English merchant ship\, The Mayflower\, left Southampton Engl
 and for the New World carrying 102 men\, women\, children and a crew of 30
 . What motivated them to embark on this incredibly dangerous journey into 
 the unknown? In addition to the passengers\; the ship\, the journey\, The 
 Mayflower Compact\, the early history of the Plymouth Colony and the ubiqu
 itous myths\, these all make for fascinating stories.\n\n Ms. Brayer has 
 a BA from Indiana University and a MA in history and education from Arizon
 a State University. She enjoyed a career in secondary education for 30 yea
 rs. After retirement\, she became a professional genealogist. She is a pas
 t president of The Family History Society of Arizona\, a member of West Va
 lley Genealogy Society\, The Arizona Genealogy Advisory Board\, and numero
 us county societies in Indiana and North Carolina. She has taught genealog
 y classes and spoken to numerous groups throughout Arizona and the West.\n
 \n Saturday\, November 21st\n\n Meeting starts at 12:30 pm\, presentatio
 n starts at 1:00 pm PST\n\n Meeting Details : The meeting is held via Zoo
 m. Login begins at 12:30 p.m.\n\n FREE Via ZOOM\n\n Register at https:/
 /www.scgsonline.org\n\n Registration closes Friday\,  November 20th
URL:https://www.scgsonline.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
