SUMMARY:Petite Landscapes in Acrylic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T220000
UID:261031wg_cv9rsHEqgYUqWBEmMWQ
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, November 21\, 2026 10:00 am to 2:00 pm\n\nLocation\
 n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nDrawing & Painting\, Workshops\n\nExperience Le
 vel\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$65\n\nM
 aterials Fee:\n\n$20\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$85\n\nHave you always
  wanted to paint landscapes but don’t know where to start? Or are you cu
 rious about acrylics but haven’t taken the plunge yet? In this class\, y
 ou’ll learn a simple technique to create small\, abstract landscapes on 
 5” square wooden tiles using a limited palette of colors.You’ll be gui
 ded through the basics of acrylic paints and mediums\, including surface p
 reparation\, color blending with a flat bristle brush\, and using differen
 t tools to add texture and detail. By the end of the class\, you’ll appl
 y a final coat of medium to seal and protect your artwork\, leaving you wi
 th 2-3 completed pieces to take home\, along with a little easel to displa
 y your favorite one.This class is perfect for beginners\, though some prio
 r painting experience is helpful. The process you’ll learn can easily be
  applied to larger paintings or even collage projects.All materials are pr
 ovided. Feel free to bring snacks or a bag lunch to eat while you work.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/petite-landscapes-in-acryli
 c-112126/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:November Soda Club Firing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T170000
UID:261031jDI7TqTxQUiBcUcCjhW_5w
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, Sunday\, and Wednesday\n\nDates & Times\n\nSaturday
 \, November 21\, 2026 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM\n\nSunday\, November 22\, 2026 
 10:00 AM – 6:00 PM \\*Time is subject to change\n\nWednesday\, November 
 25\, 2026\n\n\\*unload date subject to change based on club consensus 4:00
  Pm – 7:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nKiln Shed\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Worksho
 ps\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate and Advanced\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRe
 gistration Cost:\n\n$110\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$15\n\nTotal Registration Co
 st:\n\n$125 Prerequisites to enroll in Soda Firing Club:\n\nMust have take
 n at least one\, Intro to Mid-Range Soda Firing Workshop\n\nBe well versed
  in protocols for loading the soda kiln\, kiln safety\, equipment and oper
 ating safety\, and be willing and able to be unsupervised with the kiln du
 ring loading\, unloading\, and post firing cleaning of the kiln.\n\nMust h
 ave pre-approval from the Director of Ceramics or Soda Club Facilitator\n\
 nprogram overview\n\nThe “Julia” Soda Firing Club is designed for folk
 s looking for longterm use with our Soda Kiln\, Julia. The club is led by 
 Studio Monitors\, and a Studio Technician but involves no formal instructi
 on in soda firing processes. Without a formalized instructor\, our Soda Cl
 ub offers a more financially accessible way of having work soda-fired\, wi
 thout the need to retake our Intro to Soda Firing workshop courses. The So
 da Club will run firings monthly or as often as desired and needed dependi
 ng on participant interest. Unlike our Soda Firing Workshops\, club firing
 s will include no instruction on wadding\, slips\, glazes\, or any lecture
 s on the subject of soda firing. As such\, participants must feel comforta
 ble with the safety and care of the equipment\, as well as loading\, firin
 g\, and maintenance procedures surrounding the firing process. Each partic
 ipant gets 1 cubic foot of firing space. \\(Tip\; Make sure all your pots 
 fit approximately into a milk crate which is 1 cubic foot of space\\).\\(T
 ip\; Make sure all your pots fit approximately into a milk crate which is 
 1 cubic foot of space\\).
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/november-soda-club-firing/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
