BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma's 10th Annual Holiday Food Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T200000
UID:261111zYU8_lskQES34ulqB1WI3g
DESCRIPTION:Mon Nov 23rd 3:00-8:00 An Indoor Farmer's Market - Purchase Di
 rectly From Local Artisans & Prepare for the Holidays!\n\nholidayfoodfair.
 com for a list of vendors\n\nMon Nov 23rd 3:00 to 8:00: \\(The Monday befo
 re Thanksgiving\\) The Petaluma Holiday Food Fair is an indoor farmer’s 
 market where folks can purchase directly from local food artisans to prepa
 re for thanksgiving and beyond. This year\, for the first time\, we are ho
 sting our annual event at our distillery \\(Barber Lee Spirits\\) in downt
 own Petaluma\, where fair attendees will also have the opportunity to tast
 e our spirits and enjoy seasonal cocktails and libations while they shop a
 nd enjoy our extensive holiday decorations!\n\nFREE tickets and reservatio
 ns are required\, and will book your timeslot for entry.\n\nKids do not r
 equire tickets.\n\nAfter the 2017 wildfires devastated Sonoma County\, Lor
 raine & Michael Barber of the Brutal Hill Winery noticed that many of the 
 local artisans they supported in their tasting room were suffering from la
 ck of business. At the height of harvest season\, farmers markets were clo
 sed and sales were slim. They organized this event to get a much needed fi
 nancial boost to local food producers. The event has become a vital start 
 to the holiday season and remains an important and beloved event for local
  food artisans and Sonoma County residents to kick off the holiday season!
 \n\nSampling is up to the discretion of the individual vendors. Beer\, Win
 e\, Cocktails\, and Non-Alcoholic drinks will be available for consumption
  onsite. The number of people allowed in at one time is limited. Tickets a
 re free and include a time preference \\(15 minute increments\\) so there
 ’s less of a wait and some more space. Kids do not require tickets!
LOCATION:Barber Lee Spirits
URL:http://holidayfoodfair.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Phil Venable to present at the Napa Valley Photographic Society
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T203000
UID:261111bv5nUdundUarQg0nciXuow
DESCRIPTION:Please join fellow photography enthusiasts for Phil Venable’
 s presentation on why shooting with film can improve your photography.\n\n
 Phil Venable has been shooting photos since he was a kid\, when his dad ga
 ve him a Kodak Brownie. He studied black and white photography in college 
 and had plans to be a photojournalist until life intervened. After spendin
 g an adulthood in law enforcement\, Phil picked up my camera again and beg
 an making art. \n\nPhil’s preference is Nature/Landscape\, but he is dr
 awn to shapes\, lines\, and shadows found in the urban landscapes. His fav
 orite subjects are old rusted cars\, trains\, abandoned buildings\, and br
 ightly colored doors.  He uses several plugins to Photoshop to create sur
 real images from otherwise ordinary photos\, and creates photos in both co
 lor and black and white\, depending on subject matter and mood.\n\nPhil is
  President of the Napa Valley Photographic Society\, and a member of the F
 airfield Suisun Valley Art Association\, the Vacaville Art League\, Gold R
 ush Photo Club\, and the Lightwriters Photography Club.  He is also a mem
 ber of the Professional Photographers of America\, and the Photographic So
 ciety of America. His work has been shown at Viewpoint Gallery\, Sacrament
 o\; Yountville Community Center\, The Old Sugar Mill\, Arata Fine Arts Gal
 lery\, and the Roseville Brewing Company\, including shows at the Vacavill
 e Art Gallery\, the Napa Public Library\, Solano Town Center Gallery\, the
  Gallery at Village 360\, and he is a resident artist at The Little Shop i
 n Benicia.  He has won several awards at local shows and contests\, inclu
 ding a Juror's Choice Award at the 2013 Vacaville Art Gallery Juried Art S
 how.\n\nFor more information about the photos shown here\, or to see more\
 , go to my website at www.philipvenablephotography.com.  I am also on Fac
 ebook as Philip Venable Photography.  Contact me at philven@comcast.net.\
 n\nNapa Valley Photographic Society \\(NVPS\\) promotes the art and scienc
 e of photography\, providing education\, image appreciation\, inspiration\
 , and exchange of technologies. Most months\, we invite guest speakers to 
 evaluate our images.  Guests are welcome to attend.  Check the website f
 or more information: http://www.napavalleyphotographicsociety.org.
LOCATION:Napa Senior Center
URL:http://napavalleyphotographicsociety.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
