BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:FSVAA 63rd Annual Nor-Cal Regional Juried Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261126T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261126T180000
UID:261113UiI8KRcgskOyIUgKqfKxmg
DESCRIPTION:2026 Juried Art Exhibit: Celebrating Northern California’s A
 rtistic Excellence!\n\nFSVAA proudly presents the 63rd Annual Nor-Cal Regi
 onal Juried Art Show at the Solano Town Center Gallery – show opening is
  Friday\, Nov 13. Gallery Hours are Wed thru Sun\, 11am–6pm.\n\n The th
 ree jurors\, Ferdinanda Florence\, Nadja Fitchhorn\, and Vickie Marchand h
 ave spoken and made their selections!\n\nWe received 200 art entries from 
 67 talented artists representing 15 different cities throughout Northern C
 alifornia\, making this an exciting and impressive year for our Juried Art
  Show.\n\nIt was wonderful to see so many artists arrive with their treasu
 red works of art\, eager to have them reviewed and considered by our three
  distinguished jurors.\n\nAfter careful deliberation\, the jurors selected
  97 outstanding works of art to be included in this year's Juried Art Show
 !\n\nCongratulations to all the artists whose work was selected\, and than
 k you to everyone who participated and helped make this year's show such a
  success.\n\nEXHIBIT INFORMATION \\(Save the Dates\\):\n\n• Art Show Rec
 eption /Awards Gala: Saturday\, Dec 5\, 2026\, 3–5pm\n\n• Reception /P
 oetry Reading: Saturday\, Dec 19\, 2026\, 3–5pm\n\n• Juror's Talk: Sun
 day\, Jan 3\, 2027\, 1–3pm at the Solano Town Center Gallery  – Come 
 hear our Jurors speak! Join us as they share their insights into the selec
 tion process\, discuss what goes into choosing artwork for a juried exhibi
 tion\, and offer a glimpse into their experience. As always\, there will b
 e time for a Q&A\, so bring your questions!
LOCATION:Solano Town Center Gallery
URL:https://www.fvaa-arts.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annual Free Thanksgiving Dinner
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261126T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261126T180000
UID:26111386HFedcDk0Sio5vGh4iDhw
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, November 26\, 2026\n\nHeld annually at the **Sonoma
  Veterans Memorial Hall at 126 First Street West**. Doors open at **3:00 P
 M** and meals will be provided until the food runs out.\n\nMeals will be a
 vailable on a first come\, first served basis and all are welcome to atten
 d. There is no cost to attend\, however\, donations are gratefully accept
 ed to help offset the cost of producing the event.\n\nFor years\, the Sono
 ma Community Center\, Sonoma’s Rotary\, Vintage House and many\, many ot
 hers have teamed up to serve over 500 free Thanksgiving dinners to local r
 esidents. Led by an all-volunteer crew\, the free dinner has become a muc
 h-loved tradition in the Sonoma Valley\, bringing together a broad cross-s
 ection of the community. As always\, the meal is made using locally source
 d\, fresh ingredients and includes all the traditional Thanksgiving fare.
  Longtime Sonoma Community Center volunteer and Rotarian Gary Edwards\, a
 long with his co-chef Daniel Quijada\, lead the dinner preparations. Local
  groups and individuals including Bright Event Rentals\, Elaine Bell Cater
 ing\, Paul’s Produce\, Sonoma Market\, and Joanne Romanini Distributing 
 also donate supplies and ingredients for the event and Vintage House provi
 des all of the desserts for the dinner.\n\nPlease see website for further 
 details.
LOCATION:Sonoma Veterans Memorial Hall
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/events-galleries/annual-free-thanksg
 iving-dinner/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
