DESCRIPTION:Join us for our third “People of the West” screening\, whe
 re we watch the "Gold Rush" episode\, which covers California's mid-1800s 
 transformation — marked by conquest\, massacres\, and betrayal. Followin
 g the presentation and discussion\, participants will hear a half-hour pre
 sentation by Archaeologist Mark Selverston on research and cultural resour
 ce projects he's undertaken at prominent Gold Rush and state park location
 s. We'll then have the opportunity to take part in a gentle walk along the
  Copeland Creek Trail to the Native Plant Garden\, where we can rest and r
 eflect with nature. Dinner will be provided!
LOCATION:SSU Stevenson Hall 1301 and Native Plant Garden
