BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Remission Reimagined: Art\, Healing & Connection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T120000
UID:261114wB7pU4EhekSzAw3dNxwQIQ
DESCRIPTION:Remission Reimagined is a supportive\, community-based worksho
 p that brings together individuals who have experienced cancer and are int
 erested in exploring the role art has played in their lives. Through shari
 ng artwork\, personal stories\, creative processes\, and artistic techniqu
 es\, participants will have the opportunity to connect with others who hav
 e navigated similar experiences and participate in multi-media art-making.
 \n\nA $5 materials fee due will be collected at the start of class.\n\nAbo
 ut Cathryn Hudin \n\nCathryn is an accomplished\, professional ceramic art
 ist whose distinguished career spans several decades. She has served as an
  instructor and President of Board of Directors at Paradise Art Center and
  has taught ceramics at Butte College and California State University\, Ch
 ico. Through her participation in the Artists-in-Schools Program\, she has
  shared her passion for art with students and inspired the next generation
  of artists. A cancer survivor\, Cathryn embodies resilience and persevera
 nce\, qualities that inform her life\, her work and her endearing commitme
 nt to the arts.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center - Gallery (standing room)
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/remission-reimagined-art-h
 ealing-connection?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
