BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spencer LaJoye at Gather Petaluma - a Free\, Community Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T210000
UID:261109cYYSVXSixkifvsH6NkbQIQ
DESCRIPTION:Music for everyone: Our first concert is free!\n\nFree tickets
  required. Reserve yours at www.gatherpetaluma.org\n\nJoin us on December 
 4th as Spencer LaJoye takes the stage for Gather Petaluma’s first-ever c
 oncert - free and open to all!\n\nMeet Spencer: Spencer LaJoye makes queer
  indie folk music for all. A coast-to-coast singer-songwriter and vocal lo
 op artist with Midwest roots\, Spencer is a classically trained violinist 
 with a theater kid’s heart and a theology degree. They won the 2021 Kerr
 ville Songwriting Competition and the 2024 Songwriter Serenade\, and their
  viral anthem “Plowshare Prayer” found a home in hearts around the wor
 ld. Charming and full of banter\, Spencer will have you laughing one momen
 t and weeping the next.\n\nFriday\, December 4 · Doors 6:30 p.m. · Music
  7:00 p.m.\n\nInside the Sanctuary at Gather Petaluma\, 825 Middlefield Dr
 .\, Petaluma\n\nReserve your free ticket at www.gatherpetaluma.org\n\nWant
  to make the night extra special? Join our intimate pre-show reception wit
 h Spencer\, limited to just 12 guests. Your $100 ticket includes light ref
 reshments\, a song performed only for reception guests and helps keep the 
 concert free for all. \\(Add it at checkout\\)\n\nFree tickets required. R
 eserve yours at www.gatherpetaluma.org
LOCATION:Gather Petaluma
URL:http://www.gatherpetaluma.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T213000
UID:261108JX9OuX1fKE2wLjXP2f_VAg
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\n**Trigger warnings:** Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in
  Yiddish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mare Island Light Night - Holiday Tree Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T190000
UID:261107J2E2od32w0WGyJNC_oIygQ
DESCRIPTION:Light Night at Mare Island Friday\, December 4 | 5-7pm | Histo
 ric Core\n\nAs dusk settles over the Strait\, Mare Island glows. Come gath
 er with neighbors for our annual Holiday Tree Lighting Celebration\, a nig
 ht of music\, sweet treats\, and community spirit.\n\nSip complimentary ho
 t chocolate\, nibble on cookies\, and join us as we light the tree. Then e
 njoy a special performance by the VOENA Children’s Choir\, whose beautif
 ul voices will carry the celebration into the evening.\n\nWarm up\, give b
 ack. Bring a new or gently used coat\, or a sleeping bag\, to donate to Va
 llejo Together. Guests 21 and older who donate a coat will receive a compl
 imentary seasonal cocktail or mocktail\, compliments of The Mare Island Co
 mpany.\n\nAbout Vallejo Together\n\nVallejo Together was established as a 
 community organization in 2010 by Founder Maria Guevara to rally community
  supporters and volunteers to meet the needs of Vallejo. In 2019\, Vallejo
  Together became a fully recognized 501\\(c\\)3 non-profit organization an
 d refined their mission and vision to focus on serving the unhoused popula
 tion in Vallejo. Vallejo Together seeks to fulfill their mission of establ
 ishing reliable systems of care through collaborative partnerships\, advoc
 acy for sustainable solutions\, and offering traveling resource center ser
 vices to people without homes in Vallejo. To become a volunteer or for mor
 e information about Vallejo Together programs\, services\, and events\, pl
 ease visit www.VallejoTogether.org\n\nAbout VOENA\n\nVOENA's mission is "U
 niting the World with Children's Voices." Representing more than 35 cultur
 es\, VOENA's young singers share a message of unity\, peace\, and connecti
 on through music. Their voices have been heard on some of the world's most
  celebrated stages\, including the White House\, Carnegie Hall\, the Londo
 n Olympic Games\, and the World Expo in Japan.
LOCATION:Mare Island Historic Core
URL:https://www.mareislandco.com/news-events/lightnight2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Merry & Bright
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T190000
UID:261106phR1GfWQYEO0_GfCN3wceg
DESCRIPTION:**Step into Santa Rosa’s premier winter wonderland for the 6
 th Annual *Merry & Bright*!**\n\nPresented by Sonoma Clean Power\, produce
 d by the Redwood Ice Theatre Company (RITC)\, and hosted at iconic Snoopy
 ’s Home Ice\, this cherished holiday tradition returns with nine complet
 ely free outdoor ice skating shows. Gather the family to watch dazzling ro
 utines from professional skaters\, accompanied by classic holiday music an
 d seasonal entertainment designed to bring neighbors together across Sonom
 a and Mendocino counties.\n\nIn the spirit of innovation and sustainabilit
 y\, this year’s outdoor production is powered directly by Sonoma Clean P
 ower’s all-electric Ford F-150 Lightning truck—showcasing clean energy
  in action while helping local households discover easy ways to save energ
 y this winter.\n\n**Admission:** Completely free\, no tickets required!\n\
 n**Location:** Snoopy’s Home Ice\, Santa Rosa\n\n**Show Schedule (9 Free
  Outdoor Performances):**\n\n**Friday\, December 4:** 5:00 p.m. & 6:00 p.m
 .\n\n**Saturday\, December 5:** 2:00 p.m.\, 3:00 p.m.\, 5:00 p.m. & 6:00 p
 .m.\n\n**Sunday\, December 6:** 1:00 p.m.\, 2:00 p.m. & 3:00 p.m.\n\n**Pro
  Tip:** Arrive early to bundle up\, grab a hot cocoa\, and secure the best
  spot to watch the show!\n\nTo learn more about how SCP is giving back thi
 s holiday season\, visit: https://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays
LOCATION:Snoopy's Home Ice
URL:https://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DON LACY headlining Friday Night Comedy - Downtown Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T220000
UID:261106fMnxIJjLGUGj5fG5L5rDmQ
DESCRIPTION:Friday night stand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa with Headl
 iner Don Lacy\n\nStand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nVIP TABLES NOW 
 AVAILABLE! Snag a table for 4 with preferred seating\, your own private ca
 ll button to summon service\, and your first round of beer/cider (or a bot
 tle of wine) for only $95! Every Friday night hilarious comedians from The
  Bay Area and beyond perform at Barrel Proof Lounge. Stick around after fo
 r late-night karaoke! (This show was rescheduled from August 7th)\n\nThis 
 Week: (guest host) Tony Sparks Mitch Norton Dhaya Lakshminarayanan Headlin
 er: Donald Lacy\n\nDonald E. Lacy\, Jr. is a writer\, director\, actor\, c
 omedian\, and radio talk show host. As a comedian he was inducted into the
  Bay Area Blues society Hall of Fame in 2013. A S. F. S. U. alumnus\, Dona
 ld holds a B. A. Degree in Theater Arts\, (with a film minor). His T.V./Fi
 lm acting credits include: Cherry with James Franco\, which was released i
 n 2012\, The Other Barrio in 2014\, Denny on the NBC show Trauma in 2010\,
  'Jack'\, directed by Francis Ford Coppola\, 'Blood In\, Blood Out'\, dire
 cted by Taylor Hackford\, 'L.A. Heat'\, 'Hangin' With Mr. Cooper' on ABC\,
  'Wolf' on CBS. Stage Credits include: a 25 city tour with The Miles Davis
  Experience through Thanksgiving 2011\, “Gem of the Ocean” as Solly 2 
 Kings\, Whining Boy in the “Piano Lesson”\, Multiple characters in “
 Peoples Temple” about Jonestown\, Gambol in “Nobody Move” Alleluia a
 t Intersection\, “Hairy Ape'\, 'Good Person of Szechwan' at Berkeley Rep
 ertory Theater\, and as Carlyle in 'Streamers'. In 2006 he appeared in “
 The Shelter” at the Odyssey Theater in Los Angeles\, under the direction
  of Valery Belyakovich of the Moscow Art Theater. He also appeared in Naom
 i Izukas adaptation of “Hamlet” as “C”\, directed by Jonathan Mosc
 one. Other credits include: “Jitney”\, by August Wilson at the Lorrain
 e Hansberry Theater\, as Bennie in “Hotel Angulo”\, at the Intersectio
 n for the Arts\, “Soul of A Whore” by Denis Johnson\, and “Fists Of 
 Roses” by Phillip Kan Gotanda. Directorial credits include: 'Montage of 
 a Dream Deferred'\; 'Boseman & Lena'\; “Streamers'\; 'The Dutchman'\; 'H
 omebase' & 'The Loudest Scream You'll Never Hear'. As a playwright\, Mr. L
 acy has produced several of his plays including: 'The Loudest Scream You'l
 l Never Hear'\, a drama based on the Atlanta child murders\; 'Homebase'\, 
 a tragic comedy about crack-cocaine addiction\, and his National touring O
 ne Man Show “Color Struck”\, now in its 6th year. He also premiered 'L
 oEshe' at the 1998 Afro Solo Festival\, about the life and untimely death 
 of his 16-year-old daughter. In 2011 Donald presented his second One Man S
 how “Sexphobias” at the National Black Theater Festival. In 2013 he pr
 esented his new One man show\; How Did The World Get Here?\n\nHe wrote for
  Jamie Foxx’s pilot “These Nuts” for which he was also the acting co
 ach. Donald has written 3 feature films: “What Goes on When the Mike Goe
 s Off”\, “LoveLife”\, and “Romeo and Juliet Gettin’ Busy”. As 
 a filmmaker he has received a Bay Area Cable Excellence Award and a Black 
 Filmmakers Hall of Fame Award for his Public Service Announcement “Preci
 ous Gift.” Donald wrote and directed a short film in 2011 called Recycle
  Woman which was shown at the DeYong museum in 2012 and selected for the 2
 013 Oakland International Film Festival.\n\nMr. Lacy traveled on a 75-city
  tour with the Harlem Globetrotters as 'The Voice”. Donald Lacy as a com
 edian has been seen on BET's 'Comic View and HBO's 'Def Comedy Jam'. He ha
 s 2 comedy CD’s “Uncensored”\, & “Free Speech Costs Plenty”. Mr.
  Lacy spent his Thanksgiving holiday in 2001 entertaining the troops abroa
 d on a Far East tour that included\; Japan\, Okinawa\, Korea\, Singapore\,
  & Diego Garcia. He returned on the same tour in 2004. As a headliner\, he
  has appeared in clubs from Chicago\, to Kaiserslautern Germany. In 2007 h
 is one-man show\, “Color Struck” was a runaway hit at the National Bla
 ck Theater Festival in Winston- Salem North Carolina. “Color Struck”\,
  by invitation from Congresswoman Barbara Lee\, was also performed at the 
 2007 Congressional Black Caucus in September. In 2008 “Color Struck” r
 eturned to the Congressional Black Caucus for a encore performance. Since 
 1979\, Donald is a weekly announcer Saturdays 7 AM-12 noon on KPOO 89.5 F.
 M. \, and fill-in host on KPFA 94.1 F.M. In 2007 he was honored by the Ame
 rican Red Cross\, and in 2008 the Titan Award For Acting from Theatre Bay 
 Area. He received a broadcasting award in 2010 from Artists By Design\, an
 d in 2012 received a broadcasting award from BayView Newspaper\n\n21+ Door
 s - 7:00p / Show - 8p $15adv / $20door\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLoung
 e.com** for all sorts of good times ahead.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/don-lacy-headlining-friday-night-comedy-d
 owntown-santa-rosa-tickets-1995245772817?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Amphibians of the San Francisco Bay Area Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T160000
UID:261106GIoFKConf0-4RyrggkI3cQ
DESCRIPTION:Join the Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation for an in-depth works
 hop on the ecology\, identification\, life history\, and conservation of t
 he San Francisco Bay Area's 16 amphibian species.\n\nLed by amphibian expe
 rts Dave Cook and Jeff Alvarez\, this workshop is designed for professiona
 l biologists\, resource managers\, environmental consultants\, students\, 
 and others working with California wildlife. The workshop combines a full 
 day of classroom instruction with a small-group field trip to a private pr
 eserve in Sonoma County.\n\n The classroom presentation takes place Frida
 y\, December 4\, 2026\, from 8:30 am to 4:00 pm at the Laguna Environmenta
 l Center. Participants will also attend one field trip on Saturday\, Decem
 ber 5\, or Sunday\, December 6. Four identical sessions are available\, wi
 th morning and afternoon options each day.
LOCATION:Laguna Environmental Center
URL:https://2026amphibiansworkshop.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
