BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Matt Jaffe
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T170000
UID:261031I2fWkTZHnkC-2ui-M_sLUw
DESCRIPTION:Matt Jaffe is an indie rock & roll singer/songwriter from San 
 Francisco. Cutting his teeth on countless open mics around the Bay\, Matt 
 started taking music \\(a little bit\\) more seriously when Jerry Harrison
  of Talking Heads offered to produce his first record. Since then\, Matt h
 as continued to churn out more songs than he can remember the words to\, p
 erform on stages throughout the land \\(opening and/or touring with the li
 kes of Mavis Staples\, Wilco\, Bob Weir\, Jackie Greene\, Chuck Prophet\, 
 Melissa Etheridge\, and Blues Traveler\\)\, and collaborate with Tom Higge
 nson of the Plain White T's. Inspired by the likes of Elvis Costello\, Tom
  Petty and Stephin Merritt\, Matt is continuously writing and recording to
  build a songbook that honors his heroes.  Along with serving on Bread & R
 oses Board of Directors\, he is currently rolling out his 7th studio album
 \, Gone Enough to Miss.
LOCATION:MacRostie Winery Estate House
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109080973?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monica Da Silva & Complicated Animals
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T200000
UID:261031FkzAwQFliUW-iQKwmjV3gw
DESCRIPTION:Monica da Silva grew up living between The United States and B
 elém\, Brazil\, a city on the Amazon River. A love of travel and foreign 
 language helped to forge her unique sound. \n\n \n\nParalleling her life\,
  da Silva's music contains an eclectic mix of Brazilian and American influ
 ences. Her sound can be classified as International Fusion\, as it is heav
 ily influenced by Brazilian music\, namely Bossa Nova\, but also incorpora
 tes elements of Lounge\, Electronica\, Indie Pop\, and Worldbeat. Da Silva
  brings her cultural diversity to her songs\, smoothly flowing between Eng
 lish\, Portuguese\, and Spanish.\n\n \n\nIn 2010\, da Silva released her a
 lbum "Brasilissima" . The record featured songs in both of her native lang
 uages - English and Portuguese. The first single "Aí Então"\, “was cho
 sen by Putumayo World Music to be included on their compilation “Brazili
 an Beat”. The upbeat\, psychedelic track "That's Not The Way" was chosen
  by the music director of ESPN to be played during the programming of The 
 FIFA World Cup in 2014\, alongside major recording artists Coldplay\, Sér
 gio Mendes\, Pitbull\, Jennifer Lopez\, The Black Eyed Peas\, Stan Getz\, 
 and Astrud Gilberto. \n\nDa Silva's single "Soldado de Amor" \\(2017\\) ha
 s been featured in the BBC One series "The Replacement”\, in the Paramou
 nt Network series "American Woman"\, and in a 2019 campaign for the design
 er Tory Burch.\n\nHer music has also been featured in the series "Heartlan
 d"\, and in an ad for Patron Tequila. She is currently recording a new\, f
 ull-length solo album\, as well as writing and recording with her project\
 , Complicated Animals.
LOCATION:The Saint
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109067807?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Latkes\, Light & Luncheon: A Cooking Class at Gold Ridge Organic F
 arms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T130000
UID:261029vX274C7tSkW84PjFerOh8w
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a seasonal cooking experience celebrating the Fest
 ival of Lights that brings together the best of holiday tradition and wint
 er warmth.\n\nIn this immersive lunch-and-learn\, Stephanie Klassen Rosenb
 aum will teach you step-by-step how to achieve the perfect crispy\, golden
  potato latke paired with homemade applesauce. She will also share her sec
 rets for crafting a deeply flavorful beet borscht and demonstrate how to e
 levate simple autumn side dishes—like roasted squash—with our very own
  award-winning balsamic vinegar.\n\nAfter learning the techniques\, you’
 ll gather at a cozy communal table to feast on all the dishes prepared. We
 'll finish the afternoon on a sweet note with a slice of warm\, flaky pie 
 crafted by Red Bird Bakery\, featuring Gold Ridge Organic Farms heirloom a
 pples.\n\nWhat to Expect: A scenic ride in our apple-themed trolley from t
 he Farm Shop to the Apple Cottage • A step-by-step cooking demonstration
  inside our Apple Cottage kitchen \\(no cooking required on your part!\\) 
 • Expert tips and kitchen secrets from Stephanie Klassen Rosenbaum on cr
 afting traditional dishes using fresh\, local produce • A multi-course s
 it-down lunch featuring the day's harvest menu\, enjoyed at a communal tab
 le in our organic orchard • Seasonal refreshments\, including your choic
 e of a vibrant citrus shrub or our freshly pressed apple cider • 10% off
  all Farm Shop purchases on the day of your class\n\nStephanie Klassen Ros
 enbaum is the author of seven cookbooks\, including A Little Taste of San 
 Francisco and Honey from Flower to Table. She has taught seasonal cooking 
 at farmers markets and other venues from Brooklyn to Berkeley\, including 
 the Ferry Plaza Farmers' Market in San Francisco and the Gravenstein Apple
  Fair in Sebastopol. She has cooked at numerous artists' and writers' retr
 eats including the Headlands Center for the Arts in Sausalito\, and studie
 d organic farming at the Center for Agrocology at UC Santa Cruz.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/628485/latk
 es-light-luncheon-a-cooking-class-with-stephanie-klassen-rosenbaum
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holiday Happy Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T180000
UID:261028qyUi0-8Rek-A6bwKryUjlA
DESCRIPTION:Kick off the holiday season with a festive evening in the cell
 ar at Dutton Estate! Enjoy a selection of our favorite wines\, delicious s
 easonal bites\, and holiday shopping as you soak up the cozy charm of the 
