BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:All My Heart This Night Rejoices: The Old World Carolers in Concer
 t
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T150000
UID:261110FXdPzzI_f0WD7o0IbiyzKQ
DESCRIPTION:Since 1985\, Sebastopol’s Old World Carolers has evolved fro
 m a few folks caroling during the holidays to a choir with a repertoire of
  hundreds of songs\, but with the same authentic holiday spirit. They have
  continued to sing for peace and justice\, green energy\, human rights\, a
 nimal shelters\, homeless shelters\, shut-ins\, guide dogs\, and many othe
 r benefits for the planet and the community\, the main benefit being the p
 reservation of rare and beautiful songs in people's homes and lives. Songs
  and carols are presented in a simple way so they can be taken home by lis
 teners and sung around the house\, becoming a part of family traditions.\n
 \nHistory is an important part of OWC: learning about cultures through the
 ir languages\, traditions\, and songs\, including Basque\, Spanish\, Itali
 an\, Catalan\, Danish\, Swedish\, Norwegian\, Czech\, Ukrainian\, Old Fren
 ch\, Sicilian\, Hebrew\, Croatian\, German\, Russian\, Bulgarian\, Greek\,
  Welsh\, English\, Gaelic\, and others. They arrange many of the songs the
 y sing\, researching harmonies and styles that are proper for the place an
 d period involved. And of course\, they research and share clothing from d
 ifferent periods and regions! The usual costuming is 19th-century Europe\,
  but they have been known to branch into earlier time periods and exotic l
 ocales for special themed events.\n\nThis year the program includes carols
  from England\, Wales\, France\, Germany\, Spain\, and Denmark. The public
  is always invited to sing along\, and song sheets are provided for the en
 tire concert. The second part of the concert includes well-known standards
  for singing along. This is OWC's 41st year of singing for good causes in 
 Sebastopol. By donating at the concert or purchasing CDs\, listeners can p
 articipate in the true holiday spirit of giving to those who need it. The 
 beneficiary this year is Doctors Without Borders\, a high-rated 501(c)(3) 
 tax-deductible nonprofit bringing medical assistance to Gaza\, Sudan\, and
  many other places worldwide\, as well as Methodist charities. Listen to s
 amples and see a photo gallery at traditionalfun.org/owc. TraditionalFun 
 is a site that includes various traditional singing and dancing activities
 \, which all promote international peace and friendship and can be done lo
 cally\, without technology or special equipment.
LOCATION:Sebastopol United Methodist Church
URL:http://traditionalfun.org/owc.html
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
