BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:St Peter's Chapel Concert Series & VOENA present: Voices of Peace 
 on Earth
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T151500
UID:260922MZZe7huzPEGAE_MrZfE3Rw
DESCRIPTION:"Peace on Earth... Goodwill to All." In a world longing for ho
 pe\, there is one language that every heart understands. Hold your breath 
 as the angelic voices of VOENA take the stage amidst the breathtaking beau
 ty of original Tiffany stained glass windows. Dressed in elegant Victorian
  attire\, VOENA's singers will fill the historic St. Peter's Chapel with h
 armonies that transcend borders\, cultures\, and generations. Experience t
 he magic of the season in one of the most treasured landmarks on the West 
 Coast-St. Peter's Chapel\, the oldest Navy chapel on the West Coast and th
 e second oldest in the United States\, dating back to 1901. Surrounded by 
 glowing light\, timeless architecture\, and the warmth of human connection
 \, this extraordinary holiday celebration invites you to experience the tr
 ue spirit of the season through song\, story\, and soul. Jjoining the cele
 bration is acclaimed Taiko artist David Gonzalez\, carrying on the traditi
 on of Taiko Grandmaster Seiichi Tanaka\, the father of Taiko in North Amer
 ica. Together\, their powerful rhythms and VOENA's soaring voices create a
  universal heartbeat of connection and peace. At the heart of every VOENA 
 performance is a profound mission: Uniting the World Through Children's Vo
 ices. Representing more than 35 cultures\, VOENA has inspired audiences on
  some of the world's greatest stages-including the White House\, Carnegie 
 Hall\, the London Olympic Games\, the World Expo in Japan\, and performanc
 es for the Crown Prince of Abu Dhabi. Audiences are not simply spectators-
 they are immersed\, uplifted\, and transformed. Voices of Peace on Earth i
 s more than a holiday concert\; it is a celebration of hope\, compassion\,
  and the belief that music has the power to bring humanity together. Prepa
 re to be surrounded by soaring voices\, breathtaking percussion\, radiant 
 stained glass\, and unforgettable moments of beauty as VOENA shares the se
 ason's greatest gift: Peace on Earth.  Tickets: $50 Reserved Seating \\(Gu
 aranteed in First 3 Rows\\) $40 General Admission
LOCATION:St. Peter's Chapel
URL:https://www.voena.org/concerts/2026/12/06/peace-on-earth-matinee
