BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:St Peter's Chapel Candlelight Evening Concert "Voices of Peace on 
 Earth"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T191500
UID:260922F5nRB3CM5kKJxw64WiWmbQ
DESCRIPTION:"Peace on Earth... Goodwill to All." In a world longing for ho
 pe\, there is one language that every heart understands. Enter an evening 
 of candlelight\, beauty\, and connection as the angelic voices of VOENA fi
 ll the historic St. Peter's Chapel\, surrounded by the breathtaking glow o
 f original Tiffany stained glass windows. Dressed in elegant Victorian att
 ire\, VOENA's singers will illuminate the season with harmonies that trans
 cend borders\, cultures\, and generations. As candlelight flickers through
 out this treasured landmark-the oldest Navy chapel on the West Coast and t
 he second oldest in the United States\, dating back to 1901-you will be tr
 ansported into a world of wonder\, warmth\, and timeless holiday spirit. T
 hrough song\, story\, and soul\, this intimate celebration invites us to r
 ediscover the true meaning of the season: compassion\, unity\, and peace. 
 Also featured is acclaimed Taiko artist David Gonzalez\, carrying on the t
 radition of Taiko Grandmaster Seiichi Tanaka\, the father of Taiko in Nort
 h America. Together\, the thunderous heartbeat of Taiko and VOENA's soarin
 g voices create a breathtaking celebration of connection and peace. At the
  heart of every VOENA performance is a profound mission: Uniting the World
  with Children's Voices. Representing more than 35 cultures\, VOENA has in
 spired audiences on some of the world's greatest stages-including the Whit
 e House\, Carnegie Hall\, the London Olympic Games\, the World Expo in Jap
 an\, and performances for the Crown Prince of Abu Dhabi. Audiences are not
  simply spectators-they are immersed\, uplifted\, and transformed. Voices 
 of Peace on Earth is more than a holiday concert\; it is a candlelit journ
 ey of hope\, reminding us that music has the power to heal\, inspire\, and
  bring humanity together. Prepare to be surrounded by candlelight\, soarin
 g voices\, breathtaking percussion\, and unforgettable moments of beauty a
 s VOENA shares the season's greatest gift: Peace on Earth. Tickets: $50 Re
 served Seating \\(Guaranteed in First 3 Rows\\) and $40 General Admission
LOCATION:St. Peter's Chapel
URL:https://www.voena.org/concerts/2026/12/06/peace-on-earth
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
