BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:S.R. Laws
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T000000
UID:260312wf5j3mztGEel-jQag2GHFw
DESCRIPTION:S.R. LAWS IS OUT THERE: He approaches songwriting with a passi
 on for songs that we all grew up on. His sound rings a familiar bell in yo
 ur head while still delivering ideas completely unique.  He draws inspirat
 ion from outstanding storytellers like John Hiatt\, Lucinda Williams\, Rod
 ney Crowell\, Steve Earle\, Neil Finn\, Patty Griffin\, Chuck Prophet\, an
 d Ron Sexsmith. All of their music and others have carved a deep groove. \
 n\nGrowing up out there in Northern California\, he developed a unique con
 nection to music early on. His father worked as a trash collector\, and he
  would spend hours sifting through bags of discarded 45 records. Each find
  felt like stumbling upon hidden treasures. Some records were covered in d
 irt and grime\, while others were pristine. The thrill of discovering new 
 sounds was exhilarating\, and he could hardly wait to drop the needle and 
 immerse himself in the music.\n\nHe embarked on a pilgrimage to Texas with
  just two suitcases and $500 in his bank account. His goal was to dive int
 o the vibrant music scene and learn from fellow songwriters. Austin\, know
 n as the "Live Music Capital of the World\," offered countless opportuniti
 es for him to grow as an artist. Open mics and songwriters' nights became 
 his training ground\, where he soaked up every moment\, listening to other
 s share their stories through music.\n\nThese days\, he resides in Sonoma 
 County\, California\, working hard as a touring artist and singer-songwrit
 er for his original rock band\, The Heartsleeves. He invites everyone to j
 oin him on this musical journey\, sharing his songs one person at a time i
 n this vast and unpredictable world we live in.\n\nA.M. Sessions \n\nCheck
  out the latest album from S.R. Laws-  "A.M. Sessions." It's a collection 
 of songs that I am incredibly proud of\, crafted with the help of old frie
 nds and intrepid new collaborators. I can tell you more about it sometime.
  Come out and grab a copy at one of the shows or you can find it online. 
 “\n\n“ It is through forthright lyrics that are personal and earnest\,
  that he \\(Laws\\) composes lyrical pictures. Taking snapshots from the m
 ost common walks of life filtered through his own joy and tribulations.”
   - David Sampson - Producer Studio Secti West\n\n“..relaxed mid-tempo A
 mericana\, capturing in each song the rhythmic pocket Laws is known for cr
 eating.” -  Coyote Music Review 2024\n\n“...His lyrics simply tell fir
 st-person stories from his own life. Nothing fancy\, he's not writing to i
 mpress--he pours himself\, as is\, into each phrase and melody.”- Rebecc
 a Roudman- Dirty Cello Radio Hour KRCB Radio 104.9 FM\n\n“A.M. Sessions 
 is worth your while.” - Wiley Koepp- Texas Drummer
LOCATION:Napa Palisades Saloon
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107907400?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
