DESCRIPTION:Julius Caesar is a profound examination of the role of rhetori
 c\, the public vs. private self\, and the unforeseen fallout when a group 
 of senators takes matters into their own hands to stop a perceived tyrant.
  Shakespeare paints a complex picture of a man assassinated\, yet whose sp
 irit haunts the destiny of Rome.
