BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fright Night with Cameron Pierce & David Agranoff
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T200000
UID:261110kz2w2VXl0UyfNLWzl6nHDQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us at 6 pm on SATURDAY\, DECEMBER 12 for another FRIGHT 
 NIGHT author event with readings\, Q&A\, and signings.\n\nThis time we're 
 featuring CAMERON PIERCE in conversation with DAVID AGRANOFF for an eveni
 ng of bizarro literature. With Ross E. Lockhart moderating\, it's sure to
  be a fascinating discussion.\n\nCameron Pierce's new novel *Most Things H
 aven't Worked Out*\, just published by CLASH Books\, is a coming of age st
 ory about the painful pursuit of love\, fortune\, and fame reading like an
  optimistic Jesus' Son for a new generation. Told through a series of foll
 ies\, Pierce presents a journey of finding agency from someone who doesn't
  have an inkling of what they want out of life.\n\nDavid Agranoff's latest
  CLASH novel\, *The Last Night to Kill Nazis*\, is an emotional rollercoa
 ster of adventure\, terror and revenge that explores one of the world's mo
 st evil events through the lens of a horror novel. An entertaining and enl
 ightening novel that is *Inglorious Basterds* meets *Dracula*. Watch for t
 he sequel *The Next Night to Kill Nazis* coming in January!
LOCATION:Word Horde Emporium
URL:https://www.weirdandfantastic.com/events/6745620261212
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
