DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T213000
UID:260929nudMZN8jwUeclwFssF1K0w
DESCRIPTION:Winterlude… Handel’s *Messiah*\n\nDecember 12\, 2026\, at 
 7:30 pm & December 13\, 2026\, at 3:00 pm\n\nWeill Hall\, Green Music Cent
 er\n\n**Francesco Lecce-Chong\,** conductor and harpsichord\n\n**Santa Ros
 a Symphony Chorus\,** **Jenny Bent\,** director\n\n**GEORGE FRIDERIC HANDE
 L:** *Messiah* \\[oratorio\\] for Solo Voices\, Orchestra and Chorus HWV 5
 6\n\nIntroducing Winterlude...\, a new annual winter tradition. For its in
 augural year\, we present Handel’s *Messiah*—a cherished musical rite 
 of the season. Uplifting and joyful\, this choral masterpiece concludes wi
 th the 'Hallelujah' chorus\, offering inspiring meditation on hope and the
  promise of a better world.\n\n**Programs\, artists\, dates\, and prices a
 re subject to change without notice. Tickets are subject to availability. 
 All Tickets are nonrefundable.**
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://srsymphony.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SPe000003
 yq5FMAQ
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
